## The anti-drift trap this sweep walked into (and out of)
verify-law.ts exists TWICE — authored at packages/mpd-verify-plugin/qa/verify-law.ts and registered
VERBATIM at skills/dsh-qa/scripts/verify-law.ts. Its --self-test carries a drift arm:

  const authored   = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)          // = whichever copy RUNS
  const registered = join(repoRoot, "skills", …, "verify-law.ts")
  if (authoredSha !== registeredSha) fail("the registered case has DRIFTED …")

Run from the REGISTERED copy, `authored === registered` (same path) so the arm is VACUOUS and prints ok —
which is exactly how editing only the skills copy looks green:

$ node skills/dsh-qa/scripts/verify-law.ts --self-test
[verify-law self-test] ok: the registered copy is byte-identical (1b17a528b0db)     <-- vacuous
  (but: authored 23534 bytes vs registered 24030 bytes => identical: False)

So the authored copy was synced from the registered one, and the arm was then run from the side that
actually compares:

$ Copy-Item skills\…\verify-law.ts packages\mpd-verify-plugin\qa\verify-law.ts -Force
identical now: True
$ node packages/mpd-verify-plugin/qa/verify-law.ts --self-test
[verify-law self-test] ok: the registered copy is byte-identical (1b17a528b0db)
[verify-law self-test] ok: patch row + dist symbols + refusal vocabulary + decision/row arms
exit=0

